1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,759
Chapter 20. All a stir.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:10,317
A day or two passed, and there was great activity aboard the Peekquad. Not only

3
00:00:10,318 --> 00:00:15,358
were the old sails being mended, but new sails were coming on board, and bolts of

4
00:00:15,359 --> 00:00:19,679
canvas and coils of rigging. In short, everything be token that the ship's

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,397
preparations were hurrying to a close.

6
00:00:22,398 --> 00:00:27,119
Captain Pelleg seldom or never went ashore, but sat in his wigwam, keeping a

7
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:31,839
sharp lookout upon the hands. Bildad did all the purchasing and providing at the

8
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:35,679
stores, and the men employed in the hold and on the rigging were working till

9
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,158
long after nightfall.

10
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:42,958
On the day following Quequ signing the articles, word was given at all the inns

11
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:46,317
where the ship's company were stopping that their chests must be on board

12
00:00:46,318 --> 00:00:51,119
before night, for there was no telling how soon the vessel might be sailing. So

13
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:56,237
Quiquig got down our traps, resolving, however, to sleep ashore till the last.

14
00:00:56,238 --> 00:01:00,237
But it seems they always give very long notice in these cases, and the ship did

15
00:01:00,238 --> 00:01:05,278
not sail for several days. But no wonder there was a good deal to be done, and

16
00:01:05,279 --> 00:01:08,958
there is no telling how many things to be thought of before the Peekquad was

17
00:01:08,959 --> 00:01:14,718
fully equipped. Everyone knows what a multitude of things, beds, saucepans,

18
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:20,237
knives, and forks, shovels, and tongs, napkins, nutcrackers, and whatnot, are

19
00:01:20,238 --> 00:01:24,477
indispensable to the business of housekeeping. Just so with whailing,

20
00:01:24,478 --> 00:01:28,718
which necessitates a three years housekeeping upon the wide ocean, far

21
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:33,919
from all grocerers, coaster mongers, doctors, bakers, and bankers. And though

22
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:38,078
this also holds true of merchant vessels, yet not by any means to the

23
00:01:38,079 --> 00:01:42,158
same extent as with whalemen, for besides the great length of the whailing

24
00:01:42,159 --> 00:01:46,958
voyage, the numerous articles peculiar to the prosecution of the fishery, and

25
00:01:46,959 --> 00:01:51,599
the impossibility of replacing them at the remote harbors usually frequented,

26
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:56,237
it must be remembered that of all ships, whailing vessels are the most exposed to

27
00:01:56,238 --> 00:02:00,878
accidents of all kinds, and especially to the destruction and loss of the very

28
00:02:00,879 --> 00:02:05,679
things upon which the success of the voyage most depends. Hence the spare

29
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:11,119
boats, spare spars, and spare lines and harpoons, and spare everything's almost

30
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:14,718
but a spare captain and duplicate ship.

31
00:02:14,719 --> 00:02:18,638
At the period of our arrival at the island, the heaviest storage of the

32
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:23,679
Peekquad had been almost completed, comprising her beef, bread, water, fuel,

33
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:28,878
and iron hoops and staves. But as before hinted, for some time there was a

34
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:33,119
continual fetching and carrying on board, of diverse odds and ends of

35
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,317
things, both large and small.

36
00:02:36,318 --> 00:02:40,158
Chief among those who did this fetching and carrying, was Captain Bildad's

37
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:45,119
sister, a lean old lady of a most determined and inddehaticable spirit,

38
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,119
but with all very kind-hearted, who seemed resolved that if she could help

39
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:53,759
it, nothing should be found wanting in the Peekquad, after once fairly getting

40
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:58,237
to see. At one time she would come on board with a jar of pickles for the

41
00:02:58,238 --> 00:03:02,477
steward's pantry. Another time with a bunch of quills for the chief mate's

42
00:03:02,478 --> 00:03:07,599
desk where he kept his log. A third time with a roll of flannel for the small of

43
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:12,397
someone's rumatic back. Never did any woman better deserve her name which was

44
00:03:12,398 --> 00:03:17,679
charity. Aunt Charity as everyone called her. And like a sister of charity did

45
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:22,078
this charitable aunt Charity bustle about hither and thither, ready to turn

46
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:26,317
her hand and heart to anything that promised to yield safety, comfort, and

47
00:03:26,318 --> 00:03:31,278
consolation to all on board a ship in which her beloved brother Bildad was

48
00:03:31,279 --> 00:03:37,119
concerned, and in which she herself owned a score or two of well-saved dollars.

49
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,798
But it was startling to see this excellent-hearted Quakerus coming on

50
00:03:40,799 --> 00:03:45,519
board, as she did the last day, with a long oil ladle in one hand, and a still

51
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:50,718
longer wailing lance in the other. Nor was Bildad himself, nor Captain Pelleg

52
00:03:50,719 --> 00:03:55,198
at all backward. As for Bildad, he carried about with him a long list of

53
00:03:55,199 --> 00:03:59,759
the articles needed, and at every fresh arrival, down went his mark opposite

54
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:04,798
that article upon the paper. Every once in a while, Pelleg came hobbling out of

55
00:04:04,799 --> 00:04:09,358
his whale bone den, roaring at the men down the hatchways, roaring up to the

56
00:04:09,359 --> 00:04:15,119
riggers at the mast head, and then concluding by roaring back into his wigwam.

57
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:19,999
During these days of preparation, Quiqu and I often visited the craft, and as

58
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,477
often I asked about Captain Ahab, and how he was, and when he was going to

59
00:04:24,478 --> 00:04:28,477
come on board his ship. to these questions they would answer that he was

60
00:04:28,478 --> 00:04:33,119
getting better and better and was expected aboard every day. Meantime the

61
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:37,438
two captains, Pelleg and Bildad, could attend to everything necessary to fit

62
00:04:37,439 --> 00:04:42,638
the vessel for the voyage. If I had been downright honest with myself, I would

63
00:04:42,639 --> 00:04:46,958
have seen very plainly in my heart, that I did but half fancy being committed

64
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:51,438
this way to so long a voyage, without once laying my eyes on the man who was

65
00:04:51,439 --> 00:04:55,999
to be the absolute dictator of it so soon as the ship sailed out upon the

66
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,878
open sea. But when a man suspects any wrong, it sometimes happens that if he

67
00:05:00,879 --> 00:05:05,358
be already involved in the matter, he insensibly strives to cover up his

68
00:05:05,359 --> 00:05:11,759
suspicions even from himself. And much this way it was with me. I said nothing

69
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:17,519
and tried to think nothing. At last it was given out that sometime next day the

70
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:25,719
ship would certainly sail. So next morning Qui Quag and I took a very early start.
